# Layer 2 (profile) for `va local --profile cuda` — Linux + NVIDIA, full
# Docker-Compose stack. Sits between deploy/.env.example (layer 1) and the
# per-host secrets file ~/.config/va/deploy.env (layer 3); later layers win.
# See docs/deploy-architecture.md, "Env-Layering".
#
# The .env.example defaults ARE the cuda path (they were written for the cloud
# instance), so this profile only needs to exist as an override hook. Typical
# local tweaks — uncomment as needed:
#
# Bind local-only (default in .env.example is 127.0.0.1 already):
# SERVER_BIND=127.0.0.1
#
# Smaller GPU than the cloud instance? Pick a lighter whisper model:
# WHISPER_MODEL_FILE=ggml-small-q5_1.bin
#
# GPU pinning (multi-GPU workstation):
# WHISPER_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
# OLLAMA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
# PIPER_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0
